bber  bullets  but women are now joining forces to  protest as officers  are more hesitant to use force against  them  cold case still ahead the suspected  source of new zealand's  latest covid19 outbreak  new zealand's largest city auckland is  back in full lockdown  the restrictions were brought in today  after the country recorded four new  cases of covid 19.  new zealand had gone 102 days without  recording a locally transmitted case  contact tracing is currently underway  but as crystal commansing explains  the source of the outbreak has baffled  health officials  we know how to beat this but we also  know we don't need to look far  to see what it can mean if we don't get  on top of it we have a plan  and now is the time to follow it the  plan is simple  get tested use the track and trace app  and stay  home at noon wednesday auckland went  back into lockdown  probably is the right decision yes i  think we should  until we sort out how far it's spread in  the community  the new cases include a family of four  one of them  works for a cold storage company new  zealand health officials are looking at  frozen freight as a  possible transmission route according to  the british columbia center for disease  control  similar coronaviruses have been shown to  survive in refrigerators and freezers  for weeks and it's likely the new virus  can  also persist in cold environments we do  know the virus is spread through  droplets of an infected person  if another individual comes in contact  with those droplets or an  infected surface they can become ill  there are also an additional  four probable cases who are people with  symptoms  linked to the four community-based cases  we talked about last night  and earlier this morning all of these  probable cases are awaiting test results  until this week life had pretty much  gone back to normal  the country has just over 1200 covet 19  infections  new zealand has been able to keep case  numbers in check  through aggressive virus elimination  measures  very worried hopefully things will be  okay but  yeah very glad that the government has  moved quickly it's the right thing to do  the lockdown for roughly 1 million  people will be in place  until friday when the country's  resurgence plan  will be reassessed crystal gomansen  global news london  meantime nearby australia has recorded  its deadliest day since the pandemic  began  21 deaths were reported in the last 24  hours and all of them happened  in the hard-hit state of victoria the  country has also recorded its biggest  daily rise in coven 19 infections in  three days  with more than 400 new confirmed cases  the bulk of them are linked to an  outbreak in melbourne  australia's second largest city remains  under a strict lockdown  if you thought outdoor concerts were a  thing of the past take a look at this  the first large-scale physically  distanced concert happened in the united  kingdom  yesterday british musician sam fender  headlined  500 platforms were positioned two meters  apart to ensure fans can enjoy live  music  and adhere to safety guidelines also  perfect for those who feel anxious in  large crowds  only five people were allowed in each  penndoth area  when biden picked harris next will this  presidential pair make history  or repeat it  in november americans may elect the  first female vice president of the  united states  we've been here before the excitement  the build up the genuine belief  that history for women could be made but  life had other plans our eric sorensen  was at  both national conventions that nominated  the last two female vice presidential  nominees  he says this time's different walter  mondale beat  joe biden to the punch by 36 years i  looked  for the best vice president  and i found her in jerry ferraro  geraldine ferraro was hailed as a  breakthrough in american politics  the first woman on the presidential  ticket of a major u.s party  the issue is not  what america can do for women  but what 